    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is anchored by **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.09), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable park factor and opportunistic platoon matchups. **Luis Robert Jr.**, in particular, is positioned for a massive outing; the combination of a +16% park adjustment and an advantageous look at a lefty starter makes him our premier play. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.12) and **Kyle Tucker** (70.68) also grade as elite options. While **Kyle Tucker** is suppressed slightly by an eighth-spot assignment, his matchup against a high-ERA starter (5.48 xERA) provides the highest raw ceiling of the day if he sees high-leverage plate appearances. **Coby Mayo** (66.25) rounds out our strongest group, leveraging the same park-driven upside as **Luis Robert Jr.** to compensate for the neutral-to-difficult matchup.\n\nStrategic decisions for today\u2019s lineup hinged heavily on balancing raw power with our critical need for stolen bases. **Nasim Nunez** (42.64) was our primary bench consideration; while he offers elite speed potential against a slower delivery, his projected ninth-spot in the order and a tough matchup against Snell forced him to the pine in favor of the higher overall efficiency offered by **Liam Hicks** (41.18) and **Jackson Merrill** (45.29). We are monitoring the defensive environment closely, as **Gunnar Henderson** (61.25) faces a platoon disadvantage that offsets his park-adjusted gains, requiring us to watch for early-inning tactical substitutions. With **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** remaining sidelined on the IL, we are navigating a thinner depth chart, making it imperative that starters like **Sam Antonacci** (56.99) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.53) capitalize on their top-of-the-order opportunities to avoid stagnating our category production. **Wade Meckler** (45.95) and **Henry Bolte** (43.24) remain marginal starts, but their projected efficiency holds above our bench floor, keeping them in the mix to preserve our limited game caps while hunting for potential late-game defensive or pinch-running contributions.",
